/* book Worked example 2: Q: A pre-tensioned beam 250 mm wide with d = 500 mm (D = 600 mm) of M40 concrete has three 12.7 mm strands (98.7 mm² each, fp = 1860 N/mm²) with an effective stress of 1116 N/mm². Find Mu and check it for a span of 8 m with a live load of 10 kN/m.
   1. Ap = 3 × 98.7 = 296.1 mm². Assume fpb = 0.87 × 1860 = 1,618.2 N/mm²; T = 296.1 × 1,618.2 = 479,149 N.
   2. xu = T/(0.36 × 40 × 250) = 479,149/3600 = 133.1 mm (xu/d = 0.266).
   3. Strain check: εp = 1116/195,000 + 0.0035 × (366.9/133.1) = 0.00572 + 0.00965 = 0.0154, far beyond the elastic range (about 0.007), so fpb = 0.87 fp holds.
   4. Mu = 479,149 × (500 − 0.42 × 133.1) = 479,149 × 444.1 = 212.8 kN·m.
   5. Factored moment: self-weight 0.25 × 0.6 × 25 = 3.75 kN/m; 1.5 × (3.75 + 10) × 8²/8 = 165 kN·m ≤ 212.8 kN·m, safe.
   Answer: Mu = 212.8 kN·m against a factored moment of 165 kN·m, a margin of 1.29; the tendon yields well before the concrete crushes, so the failure is ductile. */
